url: https://0thernes.github.io/hoggar-bound-lab/
abstract: A combined study of spectral bounds and their information limits in Pauli contextuality. It
  integrates a Lean 4 formalization of the previously known spectral floor and its asymptotic 1/2 limit,
  its quaternionic (Kramers) refinement for elliptic quadrics, the five-way saturation equivalence,
  quantum-metric and two-character theorems, finite floor-saturating configurations of exact degrees 75,
  480, 2016 and 729344 plus an infinite non-closed contextual pure-CCZ determinant family |Psi_{3m}>
  (m>=1), exact CSS witnesses, double-counting ladders and unconditional Kramers-lifted bounds
  d(W(7,2))>=1455 and d(Q^+(9,2))>=6444 (paired with an independent 42-orbit C census and pure-integer
  dual check reproducing Jonah's exact triple 315, 1575, 6975), and explicit cospectral sign carriers
  whose completion spectra differ. A four-qubit C3 pair has completion cubic traces 14976 and 15360 and
  exact global binary completion minima 368 and 344 (exact gap 24, kernel-certified via pure-integer
  MET-SDP triangle-cut duals); a graph family settles case C3 for every N>=4, and variants together with
  a cone pair swap and universal cubic-trace identity settle all nine vertex cases at the
  eigenvalue-multiset level for every N>=4, proving Jonah's Conjecture E. All main theorems (110 newly
  audited declarations plus retained audits) are formalized in Lean 4 using only standard axioms,
  independently checked across multiple Lean kernels via lake comparator --paranoid, Batteries linted,
  accompanied by existential non-vacuity witnesses, a declaration-checked Lean Blueprint, and exact
  computational verifiers through six qubits. The manuscript distinguishes kernel-checked statements,
  paper proofs, executable counts, prior work, and open questions.
keywords:
- quantum contextuality
- Pauli group
- symplectic polar space
- Kochen-Specker theorem
- Clifford hierarchy
- bent functions
- Lean 4
- formal verification
- spectral invariants
- cospectrality
- Pauli completion
